# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows runner checks the tree out with CRLF and `biome check`
# fails the whole leg on line endings alone — before it has run a single test
# that says anything about Windows. The formatter's `lineEnding` is `lf`, so the
# working tree has to agree with it everywhere, not just on the boxes where the
# default already does.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched by the text filter.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.vsix binary

# The `icacls` captures are byte fixtures: UTF-16LE with a BOM, CRLF-terminated,
# and in the mojibake case not valid UTF-8 at all. The eol=lf rule above would
# rewrite exactly the bytes the parser tests exist to prove it survives.
test/fixtures/icacls/** -text
